# Discharging a verification-debt row whose obligation a machine can re-derive.
#
# The fixture drives the REAL `le commit debt-discharge` against a scratch
# checkout and judges the LEDGER it leaves behind. The row names a gate no
# verification can re-run, so `debt-clear` can never reach it: the only route to
# a non-open state is a discharge whose evidence today's producers re-derive.
#
# The last step is the one a stub cannot fake. Nothing is deleted and the record
# still says what it said, but the DEBT ROW is edited, so its digest no longer
# matches and the row counts open again. That is the fail-closed reading every
# consumer inherits from ListDebt.
#
# Both polarities of each verifier are proved by the unit tests in
# internal/le/commit/discharge_test.go, which build their own git fixtures.

option=timeout:value=60s

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze-test fixture runner/verify-scope-debt-discharge
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=discharge-fixtures-ready
expect=stdout:contains=native-debt-discharge-wrote-a-record
expect=stdout:contains=discharged-row-no-longer-counted-open
expect=stdout:contains=tampered-row-counted-open-again
